00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:02.550 align:start position:0%
 
after her breakout role on gossip girl  taylor momsen gave up acting to sing  with her band the pretty reckless  but you might not know what else she's  been up to here's what she's been up to  lately  taylor momsen entered the entertainment  industry at a very young age well before  she was old enough to make a decision  about it for herself  throughout her career momsen has  revealed that she had mixed feelings  about her upbringing  when asked about her childhood momsen  would sometimes state that becoming an  actress was her choice and that her  parents simply helped her find  opportunities but later comments  revealed a very different picture  for instance momsen said in an interview  with revolver my parents signed me up  with ford modeling at the age of two  no two-year-old wants to be working but  i had no choice  my whole life i was in and out of school  i didn't have friends  i was working constantly and i didn't  have a real life after moving to new  york to film gossip girl and finishing  high school early  momson stated that while she loved her  parents she was now legally responsible  for herself  and could enjoy more freedom and  independence it seems like momsen was  pushed into the spotlight before she was  ready and now her career is in her own  hands  when taylor momsen landed the role of  jenny humphrey on gossip girl it was her  big break  are there skins on these almonds fix it  in a timely fashion otherwise you're all  going as the real housewives of new  jersey for halloween but some of the  actors who worked with her on the show  weren't  impressed behind the scenes in later  seasons momson was appearing on screen  less and less  and tim gunn hinted at why this was  after guest starring on the show  in an interview with e news gunn who had  played a mentor to jenny on the series  said of momson what a diva she was  pathetic she couldn't remember her lines  and she didn't even have that many  i thought to myself why are we being  held hostage by this brat  while the team behind gossip girls  stated that the air time for momsen's  character was being cut for creative  reasons  it seemed likely that after working on  the series for a few years momsen was  getting frustrated with acting  perhaps gunn's characterization of her  behavior on set was unfair  but momsen was definitely ready to move  on besides i'm leaving like where i  wanted  although momson was a successful actress  she had always secretly dreamed of  making music  and after working on gossip girl she  realized that she didn't enjoy being in  front of the camera  she had been writing her own song since  she was a child and she wished she could  start her own band  one day she realized that she didn't  have to act anymore if she didn't want  to  as momsen told cosmopolitan when i  realized i could actually make my  decisions  it was a very strange feeling it was  like if i don't have to do this thing  that i don't enjoy anymore or i don't  know if i ever really did then i'm not  gonna do it anymore  because this is my life and i want to  live it and enjoy it if i can  she decided to focus on following her  passion for music instead  in her early years with the pretty  reckless taylor momsen faced some  obstacles  being a young woman in a male-dominated  genre she wasn't always taken seriously  but for a while she tried to ignore the  phenomenon of sexism in the music  industry  she was branded as a wild child for her  onstage antics and there were doubts  about her authenticity as an artist  later she realized that some of this  criticism was aimed at her simply for  being a teenage girl  momsen said in an interview with louder  sound i was so in denial for so long  about sexism but as i've gotten older i  realized it exists i've recognized it  more as i've gotten older that there is  a boys club when it comes to rock and  roll  and it is a struggle to break into that  and be accepted and treated with the  same respect as if you were a man  today she's more comfortable and  confident in her own skin  i am a female and i am psyched that  people are  liking it opening for sound garden in  2017 was one of the highlights of  momson's career  she never would have imagined that she  would appear at the same concert as  chris cornell  soundgarden's lead vocalist and one of  her musical heroes but tragedy struck  when momson received the news that  cornell had died by suicide  she told spin i was there that last  night in detroit  i talked to him at night i gave him a  hug and said goodbye  when i wake up to that news the next  morning it just went from the most  elating experience to the one of the  most devastating  after a few more performances momson  decided to put her own bands to her on  hold  she explained i couldn't grieve and  continue to get on stage every night and  pretend put on this big rock show like  everything was okay  months after chris cornell's death  taylor momsen and her bandmates were  finally ready to start recording music  again  but shortly after they decided to begin  working on a new album momson got a  heartbreaking phone call  and learned that their producer and her  close friend kato kondwala had been  killed in a motorcycle accident momsen  told metro  he was so much more than a producer he  was a fifth member of the band and my  best friend in the world  i can't explain our relationship but it  was so immensely close  after losing two people who meant so  much to her mumson tried to find a way  to numb her pain  and told the daily beast i wouldn't say  rock bottom but i was getting close to  that  i was in this hole of depression and was  not well mentally  momsen says that during this period of  her life she did not want to engage with  the outside world at  all and she spent most of her time at  home rather than turning to others for  help she tried to isolate  herself even though her bandmates lived  nearby  in the midst of her grief taylor momsen  found that even listening to music made  her feel worse the singer explained to  illinois entertainer  i got to a point where i couldn't listen  to music and that was really sad for  me if i put on any music which has  always brought me such solace and hope  and light it would bring back some sort  of memory which was too much for me to  handle  or too painful so i didn't have my  outlet which had always been there for  me  at the time momsen couldn't even bear  the thought of listening to her favorite  artists let alone writing new songs  eventually she began to pull herself out  of her depression by returning to her  favorite band  the beatles when she was able to listen  to soundgarden again she knew it was  finally time to pick up her own guitar  gossip girl fans are getting excited  about an upcoming reboot of the series  naturally the audience who tuned in for  the show's original run are wondering  which cast members might make an  appearance  fans of momsen who were introduced to  her through gossip girl are wondering if  she'll be coming back for a guest  appearance but the musician has no plans  to return to acting  momsen told the daily beast i don't have  any plans to be any part of the reboot i  never really watched the show when it  was on the air i don't really ever like  watching myself it makes me  uncomfortable  however momsen is curious about how the  reboot will handle technology  as the characters always had to have the  latest phones to spread gossip  she revealed that she's considering  watching the reboot just to see how the  writers tackle this topic  there was a time when taylor momsen  would reliably pop up in the tabloids  and gossip magazines but today she has  no real interest in chasing fame  while she loves her career as a musician  she doesn't care to put her personal  life in the spotlight  momsen revealed to people once there was  paparazzi outside my door i learned very  quickly to ignore all of it  fame is a fleeting thing just something  that you have to deal with it's not real  she may not get as much media attention  now that her days on gossip girl are  behind her but momsen is happier with  her career so the trade-off seems to  have been worth it and while momsen does  use social media she tries not to spend  too much time online in general  after going silent for a few years the  pretty reckless finally released their  long-awaited fourth album on february 12  2021. titled death by rock and roll  momsen says that although it might sound  morbid the album sums up their  philosophy on life it's a philosophy  that late producer conduala always  celebrated  living according to your own terms the  album topped the charts during the week  of its release  the fans are what make it i mean we have  the best fans with the loss of condola  it took longer than usual for the band  to pull the album together and they had  to figure out how they were going to  produce the album without him  and who they should work with instead in  addition the covet 19 pandemic prompted  the band to shift the release date  momsen told the daily beast we finished  the album right before kovid and due to  the insane world circumstances we pushed  it a little bit  as soon as it's safe to do so the pretty  reckless is ready to get back on the  road where you might be seeing a lot  more of momsen in the coming years  if you or anyone you know is having  suicidal thoughts please call or chat  online with the national suicide  prevention lifeline  at 1-800-273-talk 8255 or text home to  the crisis text line  741 741

